From 096dc940c954af4a595f86187d2094d89569b5d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 09:21:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix authentication routing: Sign In pointed at the memorial
 wizard

THE BUG, and it was not subtle: the header link labelled 'Sign In' had
to="/create". Anyone trying to sign in landed on the memorial-creation
wizard. So did anyone pressing 'Get Started'.

Two things made it invisible:
  - The real sign-in link (AccountLink) HID ITSELF whenever Supabase was
    unconfigured. With the anon key broken on the live deployment, the
    only remaining button in the header was the mislabelled one.
  - /register, /signup and /login had no routes at all, so they fell
    through to the catch-all.

FIXED
  - Header 'Sign In' removed; AccountLink is the only sign-in entry and
    it is ALWAYS rendered. Hiding the way in when auth is broken is how
    this went unnoticed; the sign-in page explains the situation instead.
  - 'Get Started' now goes to /register, not /create. Header and mobile
    drawer both.
  - New routes: /signin, /login, /sign-in for signing in; /register,
    /signup, /sign-up, /create-account for registering. Aliases exist
    because those are the paths people actually type.
  - /register is a distinct page with its own heading ('Create your
    account'), not a hidden toggle inside sign-in. It shares SignIn's
    form, so there is one implementation.
  - Switching between the two now updates the URL, so both pages are
    linkable and the Back button behaves.

6 tests, including one asserting no auth route lands on the create
wizard. 67 pass in total.
